Accurate Object Tracking Framework for Drone-Based Marine Surveillance
=====================================================================

This repository is a derivative work. It vendors and modifies third-party
source, and is distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (see
LICENSE) because that is the license of the largest vendored component.

The sections below record what came from where.


1. Ultralytics YOLOv8 (v8.0.3)
------------------------------
Path:      ultralytics/ (excluding ultralytics/yolo/v8/detect/deep_sort_pytorch/)
Source:    https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
Version:   8.0.3
License:   GPL-3.0
Copyright: Ultralytics

Vendored rather than installed from PyPI. The detection pipeline in this
project hooks into BasePredictor.write_results, and that extension point was
reshaped in later releases, so the code does not run against a modern
`pip install ultralytics`. Pinning the tree keeps the project reproducible.


2. YOLOv8-DeepSORT-Object-Tracking
----------------------------------
Path:      ultralytics/yolo/v8/detect/predict.py
Source:    https://github.com/MuhammadMoinFaisal/YOLOv8-DeepSORT-Object-Tracking
Author:    Muhammad Moin Faisal

The DeepSORT integration layer, the rounded-label annotator (`UI_box`,
`draw_border`) and the per-track trail buffer (`data_deque`) originate here.
The upstream repository ships no LICENSE file.


3. deep_sort_pytorch
--------------------
Path:      ultralytics/yolo/v8/detect/deep_sort_pytorch/
Source:    https://github.com/ZQPei/deep_sort_pytorch
License:   MIT (retained at that path)
Copyright: (c) 2020 Ziqiang

Kalman filter, Hungarian assignment and the CNN appearance descriptor.
Unmodified.

The original DeepSORT paper:
  N. Wojke, A. Bewley, D. Paulus. "Simple Online and Realtime Tracking with a
  Deep Association Metric." ICIP 2017. doi:10.1109/ICIP.2017.8296962


