Changes made in this repository
-------------------------------
Relative to the upstream trees listed above:

  - Removed the vehicle-counting logic from predict.py (line-crossing counters
    `object_counter` / `object_counter1`), leaving detection, tracking, ID
    assignment and trail rendering. The counting variant is preserved in the
    project archive but is not part of this framework.

  - Restored the canonical COCO class names in
    ultralytics/yolo/data/datasets/*.yaml. The submitted code had class 33
    relabelled from "kite" to "person" in five dataset configs. That edit had
    no effect at inference time, because class names for a pretrained
    checkpoint are read from the .pt file rather than from these YAMLs, and it
    would have silently corrupted training on COCO. See README.md.

  - Removed a duplicated `deep_sort/sort - Copy/` directory and a byte-identical
    copy of predict.py that sat at ultralytics/predict1.py.

  - Redacted a Roboflow API key that was committed inline in the dataset-download
    cell of the fine-tuning notebook. It now reads ROBOFLOW_API_KEY from the
    environment.

  - Stripped notebook outputs. In the fine-tuning notebook these were ~28 MB and
    were stale artifacts from the upstream author's vehicle dataset, not from
    any run in this project.
